<font size="4">How does Bob play 3 characters at once?</font>
<br><br>
<b>Pics reveal how it's done...</b>
<br>
<a href="images/My_setup3.jpg" target="_blank"><img src="images/My_setup3.gif" align="left" vspace="10" hspace="5" width="200" height="150" border="2"></a>You'll notice from these pics, (click to enlarge), that all 3 keyboards and mice are very close to each other, making movement from one keyboard to another relatively quick and painless, but even still, the time that it takes to move your hand from one mouse to another, then change targets to a player who is hurting, and find the spell gem to cast a heal, is often-times too slow, compared to a player who is able to stand back, watch the whole scenerio unfolding from a healer's point-of-view.
<br><br>
A dedicated healer is almost always quicker when it comes to the heals, becuase they are generally watching the pull, watching the debuffers to see if they get agro off the MT, targeting the MT for a heal, but have their mouse pointer over the enchanter or the shaman just in case they gain agro. When I play 3 characters, the healer is the least of my worries, I am pulling and making sure I get agro quickly, so that I can then quickly slow the mob with Zifnar's automatic hotkey, (praying he doesn't fizzle), and then throw a heal to Zabooboo using another hotkey, while I have Zab already targeted. 
<br><br>
<a href="images/My_setup2.jpg" target="_blank"><img src="images/My_setup2.gif" align="right" vspace="10" hspace="5" width="200" height="150" border="2"></a>The problems start when I pull more than 1 mob. I have to mez one of them with Zif, while I gain agro on the other with Zab. If Zif gets the mez off on the first try, then the hotkey to slow Zab's target is quickly hit and all is under control again. If Zif's mez gets resisted, and he starts getting beat on, I have a choice to make... Change targets with Curi, heal Zif then have another shot at a mez, hopefully not to be interrupted by the beating which is commencing on Zifnar's booty, or keep the target on Zab, throw him a heal because he's dealing with an unslowed mob.
<br><br>
You can easily see the chaos that can ensue very quickly. If I choose to heal Zifnar, and then mez the mob again, I have one chance to get him mezzed before I'm really stressed and about to give up, because Zab is needing a heal for sure by now, and Zif will be dead if the mez fails, making the mob jump on Curi for healing Zif. Her heal will get interrupted and Zab will die, then the whole group will usually perish. So, every time I pull more than 1 mob, there is a 50/50 chance the group will wipe out, when you are playing 3 characters. 
<br><br>
<a href="images/My_setup1.jpg" target="_blank"><img src="images/My_setup1.gif" align="left" vspace="10" hspace="5" width="200" height="150" border="2"></a>When ever possible, I like to add a shaman, or a dedicated enchanter to my group so they can be in charge of slows, and I can play 3, (of if another enchanter is available, sit Zif out and play 2), things go much more smoothly and the stress level is alleviated by 90%. If another cleric is available, I really enjoy the group, because being in charge of healing is such an art and a science. The timing is crucial, and full attention is required to keep everyone alive. 
<br><br>
The cleric is always monitoring the rate at which the health of the MT is being diminished, and decides which of their heal spells would be most effecient to cast, based on the beating being taken. Complete heal is the most effecient spell, however it takes 10 seconds to cast, which is not enough time depending on the ferocity of the mob. In any event, I'm always stressed out of my gord when I play 3 characters in an XP group, or on a raid, and the abundance of tells during the fights just adds to the stress, coupled with decisions that have to be made, and buffs that need to be cast, I'm lucky I get any of it right. </b></font></p>

